{
    "$comment": "Provisioning manifest for the perception models: vision, speech and the voice the speech came from. Stage F is MediaPipe's two model hand pipeline, taken from OpenCV Zoo so that it runs on the cv::dnn already linked rather than on MediaPipe's own Bazel build. The `hailo` profile holds the `-hailo` entries, compiled for the Hailo-10H against HailoRT 5.1 and run through the accelerator plugin beside the CPU set, which still covers palm detection, expression and speaker embedding; the installer ships it as a component of its own, versioned by `componentVersions.hailo`: `contents` is the sha256 of the profile's own sha256 values, one per line in manifest order, and tests/tst_modelcatalog.cpp fails when it no longer matches, which is the cue to raise `version`. The URL is a convenience and may be replaced; the sha256 is the authority. Rationale for every entry is in docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-19-cpu-perception-backends.md. The `file` names are duplicated as constants in modules/Vision/src/modelcatalog.cpp and in the Hearing module, and tests/tst_modelcatalog.cpp asserts the two agree.",
